id: pm-starter-64jd
title: Bring the coverage gate entry shim under the coverage gate itself
description: "Raising the gate to a measured 100/100/100 introduced scripts/run-coverage-gate.ts, a small entry shim that converts a thrown error into a clean message and a non-zero exit. It is NOT listed in coverageGate.sources, so the gate does not measure it and its catch branch is unverified runtime code sitting outside the gate that is supposed to be total. This is disclosed rather than hidden: the two files the gate does measure are genuinely at 100. Covering it in place is awkward because importing the shim executes the gate immediately, and spawning it as a subprocess would not report in-process coverage, which is likely why it was left out. The honest fix is probably to move the error handling into an exported function that a test can call directly, leaving the shim as a single unconditional call."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-06T20:44:17.688Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T20:44:17.688Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "scripts/run-coverage-gate.ts is either listed in coverageGate.sources and covered to 100 line, branch and function, or its error-handling logic is folded into a tested function so no untested runtime code exists outside the gate"
body: ""
